From: Korri contributors
Subject: [PATCH] x11: present VA-API frames at the current window size

The compositor can make a windowed viewer fullscreen after setup. Its output
size can differ from the encoded stream, and can change again during playback.
Use the real window geometry at presentation time, not setup's stream size.
Leave decoder dimensions and the software EGL path unchanged.

--- a/src/video/x11.c
+++ b/src/video/x11.c
@@ -61,6 +61,14 @@
       egl_draw(frame->data);
     #ifdef HAVE_VAAPI
-    else if (ffmpeg_decoder == VAAPI)
-      vaapi_queue(frame, window, display_width, display_height);
+    else if (ffmpeg_decoder == VAAPI) {
+      /* Windowed setup uses the encoded size, but a compositor can resize
+       * that window independently (including fullscreen on another output).
+       * Query here so presentation follows the actual render target without
+       * relying on input event handling or changing decoder dimensions. */
+      XWindowAttributes attributes;
+      if (XGetWindowAttributes(display, window, &attributes) &&
+          attributes.width > 0 && attributes.height > 0)
+        vaapi_queue(frame, window, attributes.width, attributes.height);
+    }
     #endif
   }
